WebGL on Haiku: an OpenGL ES context when desktop GL is too old for it

WebGL needs GLSL 1.50 from a desktop OpenGL context, or OpenGL ES 3. The
Raspberry Pi 4's V3D gives desktop OpenGL 2.1 in a BGLView (3.1 at most)
but OpenGL ES 3.1, which BGLView makes with BGL_CONTEXT_ES (haiku-pi's
libglvnd): when the desktop context's GLSL is older than 1.50, make an ES
context instead (GLContext tells ES from the version string). The view and
context creation moves into CreateOffscreenBGL() for the second attempt.

